-- Broadcasting Act 1994 (Singapore): s 2(1) "broadcasting service" and "broadcasting apparatus", s 20(1), s 47.
--
-- FORWARD-LOOKING ROW, TARGET unstable.  Not the answer of record.
--
-- The text encoded is the 2020 Revised Edition as consolidated in BA1994.txt (version in force from 25/9/2024).
-- The same provisions are in the Revised Edition 2012 (BA1994.20120831.txt) and the Revised Edition 2003
-- (BA1994.20030731.txt), both deposited; read side by side on 2026-11-03 they differ only in drafting ("shall" and
-- "no person shall" for "must" and "a person must not", "his" for "the person's"), and say the same about
-- "broadcasting apparatus" (2003: lines 198-200; 2012: 191-193), "broadcasting service" (2003: 209-220; 2012:
-- 201-212), s 20(1) (2003: 701-710; 2012: 684-694) and s 47, including the $40,000, the 3 years and the
-- forfeiture (2003: 1736-1741; 2012: 1719-1724).  That comparison is by eye, recorded here and in NOTES.md;
-- It is not a rule and not a gate.
--
-- These rules are AMBIENT: they read whatever the caller pinned (conduct day on the valid-time axis, reading
-- day on the system-time axis) through sgbau-first-schedule.l4.  The pins are written in the tests and the seat.
--
-- Order of the limbs.  Every rule below that asks "is it broadcasting apparatus" asks it FIRST.  That is not the
-- order the Act uses in s 2(1), but AND is commutative and L4 evaluates left to right, so asking first means a
-- day outside the sources REFUSES for every apparatus instead of answering FALSE for an apparatus that fails
-- another limb.  (A rule that answers FALSE outside its coverage would be wrong, not merely unhelpful.)

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgbau-nouns`
IMPORT `sgbau-first-schedule`

TIMEZONE IS "Asia/Singapore"

§ `Section 2(1): "broadcasting service"`

-- src:290 | “broadcasting service” means a service whereby signs or signals
-- src:291 | transmitted (whether or not encrypted) comprise —
-- src:296 | (a) any programme capable of being received, or
-- src:297 | received and displayed, as visual images, whether
-- src:298 | moving or still;
-- src:300 | (b) any sound programme for reception; or
-- src:302 | (c) any programme, being a combination of both visual
-- src:303 | image (whether moving or still) and sound for
-- src:304 | reception or reception and display,
-- src:306 | by persons having equipment appropriate for receiving or
-- src:307 | receiving and displaying (as the case may be) that service,
-- src:308 | irrespective of the means of delivery of that service;
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 2(1) "broadcasting service" (src:290-308)
GIVEN transmission IS A Transmission
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is a broadcasting service` MEANS
        (   transmission's `comprises a programme capable of being received, or received and displayed, as visual images`
         OR transmission's `comprises a sound programme for reception`
         OR transmission's `comprises a programme combining visual images and sound for reception or reception and display`)
    AND transmission's `is for persons having equipment appropriate for receiving it`

§ `Section 2(1): "broadcasting apparatus"`

-- src:277 | “broadcasting apparatus” means any apparatus capable of or
-- src:278 | designed or constructed for the reception of any broadcasting
-- src:279 | service and specified in the First Schedule;
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 2(1) "broadcasting apparatus" (src:277-279)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`it is broadcasting apparatus` MEANS
        `apparatus is specified in the First Schedule that governs` apparatus
    AND apparatus's `capable of or designed or constructed for the reception of a broadcasting service`

§ `Section 20(1): a licence is needed`

-- src:1425 | 20.—(1) Subject to this section, a person must not —
-- src:1427 | (a) install any broadcasting apparatus in any place, or on board
-- src:1428 | any ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore;
-- src:1430 | (b) import, offer for sale, sell or have in the person’s
-- src:1431 | possession with a view to sale, any broadcasting
-- src:1432 | apparatus; or
-- src:1434 | (c) operate or have on any premises in Singapore owned or
-- src:1435 | occupied by the person broadcasting apparatus on or by
-- src:1436 | which broadcasting services are received,
-- src:1438 | except under and in accordance with a licence granted under this
-- src:1439 | section.
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 20(1)(a), and the words of s 20(1) before it and after (c) (src:1425-1439)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1)(a) applies` MEANS
        `it is broadcasting apparatus` apparatus
    AND conduct's `installs it in a place, or on board a ship, aircraft or vehicle registered in Singapore`

@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 20(1)(b) (src:1430-1432)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1)(b) applies` MEANS
        `it is broadcasting apparatus` apparatus
    AND conduct's `imports it, offers it for sale, sells it, or has it in possession with a view to sale`

@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 20(1)(c) (src:1434-1436)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1)(c) applies` MEANS
        `it is broadcasting apparatus` apparatus
    AND conduct's `operates it, or has it on premises in Singapore owned or occupied by the person`
    AND `it is a broadcasting service` (conduct's `what is received on or by it`)

-- "Subject to this section" brings in s 20(3) (armed forces and the like) and s 20(4) (exemptions by the
-- Authority).  Neither is encoded: they are outside this row's scope (NOTES.md, coverage table).
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 20(1) (src:1425-1439)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) requires a licence` MEANS
        `s 20(1)(a) applies` apparatus conduct
    OR  `s 20(1)(b) applies` apparatus conduct
    OR  `s 20(1)(c) applies` apparatus conduct

-- "except under and in accordance with a licence granted under this section"
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 20(1), closing words (src:1438-1439)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 20(1) is contravened` MEANS
        `s 20(1) requires a licence` apparatus conduct
    AND (NOT conduct's `acts under and in accordance with a licence granted under section 20`)

§ `Section 47: the offence and what follows it`

-- src:3676 | 47. Any person who contravenes section 20(1)(a), (b) or (c) shall be
-- src:3677 | guilty of an offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not
-- src:3678 | exceeding $40,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3
-- src:3679 | years or to both, and any broadcasting apparatus installed or found in
-- src:3680 | the possession of the person so convicted shall be forfeited to the
-- src:3681 | Authority.
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 47, whole (src:3676-3681)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47 offence is committed` MEANS
    `s 20(1) is contravened` apparatus conduct

-- "a fine not exceeding $40,000": the most the court may impose on conviction.  0 where there is no offence.
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 47 (src:3677-3678)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 greatest fine in dollars` MEANS
    IF `s 47 offence is committed` apparatus conduct THEN 40_000 ELSE 0

-- "imprisonment for a term not exceeding 3 years".  0 where there is no offence.
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 47 (src:3678-3679)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 47 longest imprisonment in years` MEANS
    IF `s 47 offence is committed` apparatus conduct THEN 3 ELSE 0

-- "any broadcasting apparatus installed or found in the possession of the person so convicted shall be
-- forfeited to the Authority".  The question asked is whether, on conviction, the apparatus would be forfeited.
@ref Broadcasting Act 1994, s 47 (src:3679-3681)
GIVEN apparatus IS AN Apparatus
      conduct IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 47 the apparatus would be forfeited on conviction` MEANS
    `s 47 offence is committed` apparatus conduct
